        "checksum": "8692d076b8adeddf8d7070ec7ddd1a1036355de043b0987eb037fb1d501bf401_1_1_1_0__1",
        "ggju8zInVTd_text": "<span style=\"color:#000000;\">So we built what vets call </span><span style=\"color:#47B5E9;\">\"The Golden Middle Way\"</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;</span><br><span style=\"color:#000000;\">active cleaning without the fight</span>",
        "ggEllCIZG91_text": "<p>Brushing works because it physically removes plaque. Easy solutions fail because they never touch it. But there's another reason cats reject dental care: <strong>their Jacobson's organ</strong> — a scent-sensitive area in the roof of their mouth that makes them reject unfamiliar textures and smells. <strong>Based on research into feline oral anatomy, </strong>we created a<strong> fragrance-free finger wipe</strong> that makes <strong>direct contact along the gumline</strong>, with a soft, textured surface that gently<strong> scrubs plaque away</strong> — without triggering that reflex<strong>. Real plaque removal</strong> — in a form cats actually tolerate.</p><p><strong>No biting. No scratching. Just a routine that finally works.</strong></p>"
      }
    },
